From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 01:32:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 079/105] H1-B: fold the GDN gated RMSNorm into the out_proj
 GEMV's A-load

SGLANG_NORM_INTO_GEMV=1 (default off). The GDN block normalises its attention
output per (token, v-head) -- RMSNormGated(head_v_dim=128, norm_before_gate,
i.e. x * rsqrt(mean(x^2)+eps) * w * silu(z) -- and hands the
[tokens, 48*128] result straight to the out_proj GEMV. That norm is
`_layer_norm_fwd_1pass_kernel`: 192 one-warp CTAs moving ~150 KB, 1.88 us in
the W4 server and 1.98 us at W16, 36 launches per verify step, and it is
almost entirely on the critical path (57 us/step exclusive at W4, 68 at W16 --
see the exclusive-time analysis in the H1 report).

The GEMV already re-reads every A row once per n block, and with
BLOCK_K == head_v_dim each A tile is exactly one norm group, so the row
statistics can be recomputed from the tile that is already in registers. The
only extra traffic is the `z` tile (same size as the A tile, L2-resident at
decode widths) and the [128] norm weight; the [tokens, 6144] normalised
intermediate is never written.

Path: Qwen3_5GatedDeltaNet._norm_out_proj_fused -> Fp8LinearMethod
.apply_norm_gated -> w8a16_gemv_norm_gated. Guarded on tp_size == 1, no bias,
group_size None (== head_v_dim), norm_before_gate, contiguous [rows, 128]
x/z, swish or sigmoid gate; anything else falls back to the untouched
norm-then-out_proj path.

Numerics: the fold itself is BIT-IDENTICAL (bench/h1/h1_check.py numerics: the
norm-fold-alone column is 0 ulp at M=1/4/16) -- same fp32 order, same silu
form, same bf16 round before the dot. What is not bit-identical is the tile:
the norm is recomputed once per n block, so the profitable geometry is
BLOCK_N 64 / SPLITS 4 rather than the plain path's 32 / 6, and that split-K
re-partition moves up to 9 ulp on 0.03% of the output elements at M=16 (1 ulp
at M=4, 0 at M=1) -- the same class of change as the existing per-M-bucket
tile table. Keeping SPLITS=6 would be bit-exact but costs +0.83 us/call.

Micro-benchmark (CUPTI medians, 4x-L2 working set), fused vs plain gemv plus
the standalone norm kernel:
  M=1    12.99 -> 13.50   (+0.51, a loss: the M=1 broadcast path is not fused)
  M=4    13.85 -> 13.44   (-0.41)   [second run 13.76 -> 13.63, -0.13]
  M=16   14.24 -> 14.08   (-0.16)   [second run 14.11 -> 14.24, +0.13]
So in isolation this is a wash, +-0.3 us of run-to-run noise. The reason to
measure it in the server anyway is that the norm kernel costs 1.9-2.0 us there
against 1.3-1.5 us here, and one launch of 1543 disappears.

Also swept (bench/h1/h1_check.py optune) whether the plain tiles for the three
biggest critical-path shapes have any headroom: they do not. o_proj, qkvz and
attn_qkv are all within 0.13 us/call of the server's current plan at M=1/4/16
(the one exception, attn_qkv (64,128,1,4w,4s) at M=16, -0.83 us here, is the
config the tuning table already pins away from because the server disagreed).

